      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T05:21:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect this problem occurs because EM stays alive long enough after fru-device/gpio-presence exit to finish a rescan. One possible reason is that the dbus-sensors units order themselves after EM (e.g. [the ADC sensor service]), so EM\u0027s shutdown may wait for them, while fru-device and gpio-presence have no such ordering.\n\nAlso, EM configs may probe objects from other services, so ordering EM after a fixed set of services may not cover all cases. I\u0027m not sure service file ordering alone fully addresses the issue and would like to hear other opinions.\n\n[the ADC sensor service]: https://github.com/openbmc/dbus-sensors/blob/393c0f71be63cc59b8c345126ed53c99a333ecec/service_files/xyz.openbmc_project.adcsensor.service#L6",
      "revId": "f7941e032fb7b75389d5d776500a02d2e3687652",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c82dca2_308c77ed",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001712
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T13:18:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For guaranteed coordination, PSM could explicitly request and await shutdown preparation before starting BMC reboot.\n\nFor example by making a mapper call to see which services have an interface that\ncan be used for shutdown preparation, and then calling a method `PrepareForShutdown()` on that interface for all these services.\n\nThe services could then unsubscribe from most of their D-Bus matches or set a flag for their match handlers to avoid any activity or event logs caused from other services being stopped.\n\ni have not checked this idea against any designs that may or may not exist for this purpose so please take it with a grain of salt.\n\n\nOverall i believe you hit the nail on it\u0027s head. Due to it\u0027s design, EM can have a dependency cycle with various other services. EM provides the config, the other service speaks some protocol with the device or does it\u0027s own probing and then publishes it\u0027s own interfaces on which EM can then also probe.\n\nSo no matter which one is shut down first, it could result in some unexpected event logs. The alternative would be a staged global shutdown phase where reactors stop processing most of their D-Bus matches.\n\nNot sure if that is too much work or the wrong idea when this patch could solve the issue for the most common scenario.",
      "parentUuid": "b7f22004_d4dbce71",
      "revId": "f7941e032fb7b75389d5d776500a02d2e3687652",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
